{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Looking for a Job"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " One Step More ..."}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "voice"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "opinion, point of view"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to write stories that express the voice of a person."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le03ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about online journalism."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "high standards"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expectations for quality"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This has inspired me to maintain high standards for content."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le03ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "traffic flow "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "number of people visiting a website"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The vast majority of traffic flow for news -- over 80% -- is going to established, credible sources."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le03ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sources"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "places where a person gets the information they need to make decisions and form opinions "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, they are still heading towards traditional news sources, expecting to get accurate information. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le03ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "informative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "contains a lot of useful information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have always felt confident there will always be an audience for a well written, informative story. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le03ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "confines"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " boundaries; limits"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is up to journalism to break us out of those confines."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le03ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Reason: <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use -ing clauses to express reason."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A clause is a part of a sentence with its own subject and verb. You can use verb+ing in a clause to express reason, relationships, or to explain <span class=\"italic\">why</span> something happened. It also allows you  to be very specific about the relationship between the two clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">When I was a boy, publishers came running after you, hoping to find someone who could put a sentence together. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is an alternative to using typical words like<span class=\"italic\"> because </span>and <span class=\"italic\">since</span> to give the reason. <br/><br/>For example, instead of saying <br/><span class=\"italic\"> When I was a boy, publishers came running after you <span class=\"strong\">because</span> they hoped to find someone who could put a sentence together. </span> <br/>You can use the sentence above. <br/><br/>Varying your style of writing and speech is beneficial in workplace setting as it gives you and your ideas a more dynamic feel and livens up otherwise simplistic language."}, {"type": "example", "content": "People are still heading towards traditional news sources, expecting to get accurate information. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Newspapers have invested significant sums of money, wanting their online presence to grow even further. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect, Simple Present and Present Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a variety of tenses in speaking and writing. Let's compare the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>, the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> Tenses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about a past action with present consequences. You often use it to refer to experiences that you have and are related to a present task or situation.  </br></br>For example:</br></br><span class=\"italic\">  This <span class=\"strong\">has inspired</span> me to maintain high standards for content in journalism."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> tense to talk about a habit or an event scheduled in the future.</br></br> For example:</br></br><span class=\"italic\">  We all <span class=\"strong\">live</span> in our own worlds and we all <span class=\"strong\">love</span> to think that we are educated and cultured. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to refer to things that are happening at the moment of speaking or planned future events.  </br></br>For example: </br></br><span class=\"italic\"> People <span class=\"strong\">are getting</span> their news from online media more now than ever.</span>"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask people about where they get news."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare a diagram with the results of the survey."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the results to a partner or to a group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I interpret the results."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ask 10 - 15 people where they get most of their news. For example, do they read a printed newspaper? Do they read articles online? Do they listen to the radio?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compile the results of your survey (count the number of people who answered the same thing)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a diagram, like a bar graph, to show your results."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your diagram to a partner or to the class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to interpret (explain) the results.  What does the graph show? Why is this the case?"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le03ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le03ob07re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le03ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Well, you are quite the determined young man.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: A person has to be in today's job market, Mr. Brody.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: When I was a boy, publishers came running after you, hoping to find someone who could put a sentence together. Why do you want to be a journalist?\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I want to write stories that express the voice of a person who otherwise would not be heard, to a large audience.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Why do you want to work with online content?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le03ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: People are getting their news from online media more now than ever. However, they are still heading towards traditional news sources, expecting to get accurate information. This has inspired me to maintain high standards for content. It is a way of promoting a publication's reputation and brand.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Are you optimistic about the future of journalism?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Yes, absolutely. The vast majority of traffic flow for news -- over 80% -- is going to established, credible sources. Some media sources have seen their audience increase. They have invested significant sums of money, wanting their online presence to grow even further. I have always felt confident there will always be an audience for a well written, informative story.", "id": 2, "time": "24000", "image": "engenn10le03ob07re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: What would you say is the purpose of journalism?\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: We all live in our own worlds and we all love to think that we are educated and cultured. Nonetheless, we are still the products of our environment, wanting to follow the same pattern day after day. It is up to journalism to break us out of those confines and let us hear about the issues and the events, and most importantly, the voices of people who are beyond the boundaries of our day-to-day lives.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Very impressive, young man. Please bring in two letters of reference.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I will do that right away, Mr. Brody.", "id": 3, "time": "69000", "image": "engenn10le03ob07re2img07.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about jobs, professions and careers."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about my experiences. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "co